<!DOCTYPE node PUBLIC
"-//freedesktop//DTD D-Bus Object Introspection 1.0//EN"
"http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd">
<!--
  Peer-to-peer D-Bus interface between coffee-rdp-session (client, one per
  connection) and the resident coffee-rdp-auth serve helper (server, one
  per running coffeerdp instance). Not a session-bus service: there is no
  well-known bus name here, this is spoken over a private GDBusServer
  listening on a unix socket at $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/coffeerdp/auth.sock (see
  PLAN.md Phase 7.5). gdbus-codegen still applies identically to P2P
  connections, so the generated skeleton/proxy pair is used exactly as it
  would be for a bus service.
-->
<node name="/com/codeneedscoffee/coffeerdp/Auth1">
 <interface name="com.codeneedscoffee.coffeerdp.Auth1">
  <!--
    Runs (or reuses) the resident AAD/AVD login WebView against `url`,
    attempting a hidden, off-screen load first and only presenting a visible
    window if the server doesn't answer the redirect within a short window
    (see coffee-rdp-auth's ScheduleReveal). Blocks for as long as an actual
    interactive login takes: there is deliberately no client-side timeout
    here beyond what GDBus itself imposes when told to wait indefinitely.

    `password`: resolved plaintext from a profile's 1Password reference
    (coffee_profiles.hpp's onePasswordRef), or empty. When non-empty, the
    helper best-effort autofills Microsoft's own password field once the
    page loads and submits it; empty means "no reference configured (or
    `op read` failed)", in which case the page behaves exactly as it did
    before this existed: ordinary interactive login. A wrong password is
    never retried automatically (see coffee_rdp_auth.cpp's tryAutofill),
    only attempted once per request. Passed as a plain D-Bus argument
    rather than embedded in `url` because this is the private peer-to-peer
    socket (0700 dir, PLAN.md Phase 7.5) already used for the OAuth code
    itself: no new exposure. The one-shot spawned path (webview_impl.cpp,
    used when no resident helper is reachable) carries the equivalent value
    via an env var instead of argv, since /proc/PID/cmdline is
    world-readable on a stock install while /proc/PID/environ isn't.

    `op_item_ref`: the profile's raw op://vault/item/field reference
    (coffee_profiles.hpp's onePasswordRef), unresolved, or empty. Not
    secret: this is the same reference already accepted as safe to keep
    in plaintext in profiles.ini, but threaded the same env-var-not-argv
    way as `password` for the spawned path anyway, for consistency rather
    than special-casing it. Used to resolve the MFA/verification-code step
    (see coffee_rdp_auth.cpp's resolveOtpCode() for the exact `op` command)
    at the moment that field actually appears rather than up front like
    `password`: a TOTP code expires in about 30 seconds, so resolving it
    early risks submitting a stale one by the time the page gets there.
  -->
  <method name="RequestToken">
   <arg type="s" name="url" direction="in"/>
   <arg type="s" name="title" direction="in"/>
   <arg type="s" name="password" direction="in"/>
   <arg type="s" name="op_item_ref" direction="in"/>
   <arg type="s" name="code" direction="out"/>
  </method>
  <!--
    Asks the resident helper to exit after any in-flight RequestToken call
    finishes. Sent by the connection manager on a real, explicit quit (not
    on ordinary window-close, see Phase 7.5's background-portal design) so
    the helper doesn't outlive the app that owns it.
  -->
  <method name="Quit">
  </method>
 </interface>
</node>
